---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import { getTranslations, localePath } from '../../i18n/ui';

const locale = 'en';
const t = getTranslations(locale);
const updated = 'August 8, 2026';
const privacyPath = localePath(locale, 'privacy');
---

<BaseLayout locale={locale} title={t.legal.termsTitle} description={t.legal.termsTitle}>
  <Header locale={locale} />
  <main class="section-padding pt-44">
    <article class="container-main max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="heading-soft mb-2 text-3xl font-bold">{t.legal.termsTitle}</h1>
      <p class="mb-8 text-xs text-text-dim">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the Auroboros Soft website (the "Site") and the
          provision of trading bot software and related services ("Software", "bot", "services"). By using the
          Site, submitting a request, or purchasing our products and services, you confirm that you have read and
          accept these Terms.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">1. Parties and definitions</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-text">Provider</strong> — Auroboros Soft, offering Software and services through
            the Site.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            <strong class="text-text">User / Client</strong> — any individual or legal entity that visits the Site,
            submits a request, or uses purchased Software.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            <strong class="text-text">Ready-made products</strong> — software for automated trading listed in the
            Products section of the Site, including MOEX PRO, CRYPTO PRO, and any other ready-made bots or related
            materials we publish on the Site at the time of your order.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            <strong class="text-text">Custom development</strong> — building or adapting a trading bot to the Client's
            requirements.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">2. Services</h2>
          <p>The Provider offers:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>ready-made trading bot Software for supported platforms;</li>
            <li>custom development, configuration, and adaptation;</li>
            <li>consultations on installation, setup, and operation;</li>
            <li>technical support — within the scope agreed at the time of order.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Specific scope, timelines, pricing, and delivery method are agreed when your request is processed and may
            be recorded in correspondence, an invoice, contract, or other document as agreed.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">3. Use of the Site</h2>
          <p>When using the Site, you agree to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>provide accurate information in the contact form;</li>
            <li>not disrupt the Site or attempt unauthorized access to systems;</li>
            <li>not use Site materials in violation of copyright or without the Provider's consent;</li>
            <li>comply with applicable law and the rules of trading platforms used with the Software.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            The Provider may restrict access or decline to process a request in case of violation of these Terms or
            suspected abuse, spam, or fraud.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">4. No investment advice</h2>
          <p>
            Information on the Site, in product descriptions, FAQ, and correspondence is informational and technical.
            We are not an investment adviser, broker, or asset manager. We do not tell you what to buy or sell: the
            bot executes predefined rules. Trading decisions, instrument selection, position size, and risk settings
            are yours alone.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">5. Trading risks</h2>
          <p>
            Trading financial markets involves the risk of losing capital. The bot does not guarantee returns — results
            depend on the market, settings, connectivity to the exchange or broker, and your decisions. A successful
            backtest, demo, or test run does not mean future results will be the same.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            You acknowledge that using the Software does not eliminate losses, slippage, connectivity failures,
            exchange rule changes, or other market and technical risks. We recommend starting with conservative
            settings and sizes that match your financial situation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">6. Software operation and technical risks</h2>
          <p>
            The trading bot is software. It may contain errors, stop working, work partially, or behave differently
            from what is described on the Site or what the Client expects — for any reason, including code defects,
            hardware or OS incompatibility, internet or server failures, exchange or broker API changes, third-party
            software updates, misconfiguration, actions of third parties, or force majeure.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            The Provider does not guarantee that the Software will run without interruption, without errors, or in
            line with your expectations. We are not liable if the bot fails to start, stops working, behaves
            incorrectly, or produces results different from what you expected. All risks related to installation,
            configuration, operation, and consequences of using the Software are borne by the Client.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">7. License and intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            All Site materials (text, design, logos, descriptions, source and compiled Software code) belong to the
            Provider or are used under lawful rights. The Client receives a non-exclusive right to use purchased
            Software according to the order terms. For ready-made bots, unless agreed otherwise: one license key
            is for activation on one Client computer.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">Without written consent from the Provider, the Client may not:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>copy, distribute, resell, or sublicense the Software to third parties;</li>
            <li>decompile, modify, or create derivative products based on the Software, unless agreed separately;</li>
            <li>remove or hide authorship or usage restrictions.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">8. Orders, payment, and delivery</h2>
          <p>
            Requests are accepted via the Site form or email. Price, payment method, and delivery timeline are agreed
            individually. Until payment is received (unless otherwise agreed), the Provider may withhold files, access
            keys, or other Software materials.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Delivery may be by electronic means (archive, link, repository, etc.). The Client must be able to receive
            materials and keep any access credentials confidential.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">9. Client responsibilities</h2>
          <p>The Client is solely responsible for:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>risk settings, limits, and instrument selection;</li>
            <li>compliance with exchange, broker, or platform rules;</li>
            <li>suitable hardware, OS, internet connection, and accounts;</li>
            <li>backing up settings and monitoring the bot in live trading;</li>
            <li>tax and other applicable laws in their jurisdiction.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">10. Support and updates</h2>
          <p>
            Support scope (consultations, fixes, updates) is defined by the specific order. For ready-made MOEX pro
            and CRYPTO pro bots, free technical support for first launch is provided for 30 calendar days from
            delivery unless otherwise agreed. We aim to respond
            promptly but do not guarantee uninterrupted operation when exchanges, broker terminals, or third-party
            software change. Adaptation timelines may be agreed separately.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">11. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            Software and services are provided "as is" to the extent permitted by law. The Provider is not liable for
            Software failures, errors, or incorrect operation (including the cases described in Section 6), trading
            losses, lost profits, indirect or incidental damages arising from use or inability to use the
            Software, actions of third parties (exchanges, brokers, connectivity providers), or Client decisions.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Total liability for any claim related to a specific order is limited to the amount actually paid by the
            Client for that product or service, unless mandatory law requires otherwise.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">12. Refunds</h2>
          <p>
            Because Software is digital, refunds after files, keys, or access have been delivered are generally not
            provided unless explicitly agreed or required by mandatory law. If a material technical defect is confirmed
            by the Provider, the parties will agree on a fix, replacement, or other remedy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">13. Personal data</h2>
          <p>
            Processing of personal data is governed by our{' '}
            <a href={privacyPath} class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>. By submitting a request,
            you confirm that you have read it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">14. Changes to these Terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these Terms. The current version is always on this page with the date at the top. Continued
            use of the Site or Software after changes means you accept the updated Terms, unless applicable law
            requires otherwise.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">15. Governing law and disputes</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the Russian Federation unless otherwise agreed in a separate
            contract. Disputes should first be resolved through negotiation; if that fails, they may be submitted to
            a court at the Provider's location unless mandatory rules provide otherwise.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="heading-soft mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">16. Contact</h2>
          <p>For questions about these Terms, orders, or support:</p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Email:{' '}
            <a href="mailto:auroboros.soft@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">auroboros.soft@gmail.com</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <a href={localePath(locale)} class="mt-8 inline-block text-primary hover:underline">{t.legal.backHome}</a>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer locale={locale} />
</BaseLayout>
